9. Key Takeaways

- A VPC is a logically isolated AWS network.
- A subnet is a network segment within a VPC and belongs to one AZ.
- A VPC's "Available" state does not confirm internet connectivity.
- Region and AZ are different concepts.
- Multiple AZs can improve availability when the architecture is configured correctly.
- A public subnet requires appropriate routing and other network settings to support internet connectivity.
- Route Tables and Internet Gateways must be verified together when troubleshooting public access.
